          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 6"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.12,
            0.886,
            0.188
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Z, P and T. These points are read as ‘Point Z’, ‘Point P’ and ‘Point T’. Of course, the dots represent precise locations and must be imagined to be invisibly thin."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.17,
            0.216,
            0.422,
            0.241
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2.2 Line Segment"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.255,
            0.645,
            0.323
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Fold a piece of paper and unfold it. Do you see a crease? This gives the idea of a line segment. It has two end points, A and B."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.324,
            0.646,
            0.391
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Mark any two points A and B on a sheet of paper. Try to connect A to B by various routes (Fig. 2.1)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.392,
            0.648,
            0.53
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What is the shortest route from A to B? This shortest path from point A to Point B (including A and B) as shown here is called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "line segment",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " from A to B. It is denoted by either AB or BA. The points A and B are called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "end points",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of the line segment AB."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.655,
            0.243,
            0.88,
            0.497
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.655,
                0.243,
                0.88,
                0.497
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_1_image_6.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.756,
                0.499,
                0.82,
                0.517
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 2.1"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.17,
            0.555,
            0.292,
            0.58
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2.3 Line"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.596,
            0.66,
            0.731
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Imagine that the line segment from A to B (i.e., AB) is extended beyond A in one direction and beyond B in the other direction without any end (see Fig. 2.2). This is a model for a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "line.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Do you think you can draw a complete picture of a line? No. Why?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.678,
            0.581,
            0.884,
            0.71
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 10,
              "bbox": [
                0.678,
                0.581,
                0.884,
                0.71
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_1_image_10.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.731,
            0.885,
            0.799
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A line through two points A and B is written as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\overrightarrow { \\mathrm { A B } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . It extends forever in both directions. Sometimes a line is denoted by a letter like l or m."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.801,
            0.885,
            0.846
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Observe that any two points determine a unique line that passes through both of them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
